{
  "$schema": "https://openapi.vercel.sh/vercel.json",
  "_comment": [
    "NOT named vercel.json, and it must stay that way.",
    "",
    "A vercel.json at the repo root fails the SITE project's deployment at",
    "config time, even though that project's Root Directory is web-next: the",
    "`functions` pattern below matches no function inside web-next. This was",
    "confirmed twice, most recently on 2026-07-27, when a functions-only",
    "version still failed the build. tests/test_api_advisor.py enforces the",
    "absence of the real filename.",
    "",
    "This file therefore records the settings to apply BY HAND in the Vercel",
    "dashboard for the advisor project (a second project on this repository,",
    "Root Directory = repo root, which deploys api/advisor.py as a Python",
    "function). Vercel detects Python from the .py extension with no config.",
    "",
    "Settings > Functions: max duration 300s. A real generation measured 53s,",
    "and counter builds with a full enemy team run longer, so the Hobby 60s",
    "cap is not enough headroom; 300s needs a plan above Hobby.",
    "",
    "Dependencies come from the repo-root requirements.txt, kept down to",
    "`requests` because the bundle limit is 250MB unzipped. Scraper deps are",
    "in requirements-scrape.txt.",
    "",
    "Do NOT set functions.runtime: it is only valid for community runtimes and",
    "an invalid value fails config validation."
  ],
  "functions": {
    "api/advisor.py": {
      "maxDuration": 300,
      "memory": 1024
    }
  }
}
